      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 554,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound made up of two elements: **hydrogen** and **oxygen**. Its chemical formula is **$H_2O$**, meaning every single molecule of water consists of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom. \n\nHowever, water is much more than just a chemical formula. It is the defining substance of our planet and the foundation of all known life. \n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is, based on its states, properties, and importance:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Three States of Matter\nWater is one of the few substances on Earth that naturally exists in three distinct forms (states) depending on the temperature:\n*   **Liquid:** The standard form we drink, swim in, and use for rain (found in oceans, rivers, and lakes).\n*   **Solid (Ice):** Formed when water freezes at or below 0°C (32°F). Ice is unique because it is *less dense* than liquid water, which is why ice floats.\n*   **Gas (Vapor/Steam):** Formed when water heats up and evaporates or boils at 100°C (212°F). \n\n### 2. Unique Chemical Properties\nWater has several unusual and remarkable properties that make it essential for life:\n*   **The \"Universal Solvent\":** Because of its chemical structure, water can dissolve more substances (like salt, sugar, and minerals) than any other liquid. This allows it to carry nutrients and chemicals through living things and ecosystems.\n*   **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat before its temperature changes significantly. This helps regulate the climate of the Earth and keeps living organisms from overheating.\n*   **Cohesion and Adhesion:** Water molecules like to stick to each other (**cohesion**—which creates surface tension, allowing some bugs to walk on water) and to other surfaces (**adhesion**—which allows water to move up the roots of tall trees against gravity).\n\n### 3. Importance to Life\n*   **Biological Necessity:** Life as we know it cannot exist without water. The human body is made up of about 60% water. It cushions our joints, regulates our internal temperature, and transports nutrients in our blood.\n*   **Habitat:** Water covers about **71% of the Earth's surface**, mostly in oceans, and provides a home for millions of aquatic species.\n\n### Summary\nIn short, water is a simple molecule with extraordinary properties. It sculpts the Earth's landscape, drives our weather and climate, and flows through the veins of every living thing."
